# Memory-sidecar recovery — lifespan-leak fix + reference_time schema migration

2026-04-29. Closes the two coupled defects the diagnostic agent
surfaced 2026-04-29 (`.scratch/claude-output/memory-sidecar-
diagnostic.md`):

1. **Lifespan-leak.** `service.lifespan()`'s `finally` block at
   service.py:115 set `_graphiti = None` on every session close.
   FastMCP routes the user lifespan to `MCPServer.run`, which is
   invoked PER MCP session by `StreamableHTTPSessionManager`. Each
   session close therefore nulled `_graphiti`, defeating
   `_ensure_graphiti()`'s idempotency guard. The next session
   rebuilt the Graphiti driver, opening another `kuzu.Database`
   against the same on-disk file. Kuzu's 8 TiB virtual mmap
   reservation accumulated per session; mmap eventually failed on
   macOS VA fragmentation; the sidecar entered a permanent stuck
   state returning 503 forever. Fix: drop the `_graphiti = None`
   line. Driver lives for process lifetime; `close()` runs only
   at actual process shutdown via the lifespan's outer try/finally
   (still preserved).

2. **Schema-migration.** `add_episode` failed with `Binder
   exception: Cannot find property reference_time for e.` The
   on-disk `kuzu_db` (created against an older graphiti-core)
   lacked `reference_time TIMESTAMP` on `RelatesToNode_`. Current
   graphiti-core 0.28.x writes that column; `CREATE NODE TABLE IF
   NOT EXISTS` is a no-op when the table exists, so the column
   never got retro-added. Fix: idempotent `ALTER TABLE ADD IF NOT
   EXISTS reference_time TIMESTAMP` on each boot, alongside the
   existing D10 `retention_class` migration. Kuzu 0.11+ supports
   the IF NOT EXISTS form (verified empirically at plan time).

The fixes interact: any rebuild-from-`episodes.json` path would
tear down + reinitialize the driver, re-triggering fix #1's leak.
So ALTER TABLE (not rebuild) is the right shape for #2; #1 lands
first conceptually.

Structural remedy:

  - `framework/memory-system/src/service.py:115` — drop
    `_graphiti = None` from the lifespan's `finally` block.
  - `framework/memory-system/src/service.py:91` — replace
    `await _graphiti.build_indices_and_constraints()` with
    `await prepare_graphiti(_graphiti)`. This routes the
    sidecar's startup path through both schema migrations
    (reference_time + retention_class). Closes the latent hole
    where the sidecar's startup never added the D10
    retention_class column unless `MemoryAPI` ingest paths
    exercised it (HSF#1 in plan §16).
  - `framework/memory-system/src/retention.py` — extend with
    `ENSURE_REFERENCE_TIME_COLUMN_CQL` constant +
    `ensure_reference_time_column(driver)` async helper. Same
    shape as the existing `ensure_retention_column`.
  - `framework/memory-system/src/factory.py::prepare_graphiti` —
    call the new helper after the existing
    `ensure_retention_column` call.

Sealed-test in-band retire (ODD §4 per `feedback_loose_AC_text_
fix_AC_not_implementation`):

  - `tests/test_service.py:183` — `assert service._graphiti is
    None` retires to `assert service._graphiti is fake`. AC24.1's
    actual spec text is "constructs Graphiti exactly once, calls
    build_indices_and_constraints, yields, and calls close
    exactly once on exit"; the "module global cleared on exit"
    assertion was over-specification beyond the AC.
  - `tests/test_AC34_eager_health_after_startup.py:293` — same
    edit. AC34.2's pointer-to-evidence inline check inherited the
    loose assertion from AC24.1.

AC surface (AC.MS-FIX.1..MS-FIX.5 + AC.MS-FIX.S):

  - AC.MS-FIX.1: lifespan no longer nulls `_graphiti` on session
    close. Mock-test using FakeGraphiti.
  - AC.MS-FIX.2: `ensure_reference_time_column` is idempotent.
    In-process kuzu unit test.
  - AC.MS-FIX.3: `_ensure_graphiti` calls `prepare_graphiti`.
    Source-grep + mock-test exercise.
  - AC.MS-FIX.4: sealed-test text update at the two named lines.
  - AC.MS-FIX.5: operational verification — health 200,
    add_episode works, search works post-launchctl-kickstart.
  - AC.MS-FIX.S: seal-diff invariant — only paths under
    `framework/memory-system/` or universal-paths.

Method-level choices (builder's call per ODD §1.1):

  - Test shape (D4): in-process mock test over subprocess. The
    existing AC34.1 subprocess test covers the production entry
    point structurally; a second subprocess test gains no
    marginal coverage.
  - Schema-migration call site (D2): co-locate with existing D10
    retention-class migration in `retention.py`. Sibling helper
    + sibling call from `prepare_graphiti`.
  - Schema-migration call point (D3): inject into
    `_ensure_graphiti` (one-line replacement of the existing
    `build_indices_and_constraints` call). Closes the latent
    retention-class hole as a side effect.

Out of scope (per plan §8):

  - Per-session lifespan model (FIDRAFT-tracked structural
    concern; deferred to v0.1.1+).
  - Log rotation for `graphiti-service.err.log` (FIDRAFT-tracked).
  - launchd label `com.pos-v2.*` → `com.loam.*` rename
    (M1c-corrective task #16; separate amendment).
  - `KuzuDriver.close()` unmap verification (FIDRAFT-tracked).
  - retention.py rename to schema_migrations.py (sealed-component
    rename, no immediate value).
  - M6c's graceful-fallthrough-with-detection CDC retroactive
    operationalisation across memory-system (FIDRAFT-tracked per
    dispatch trigger #5).

